From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] application: no 10 s full redraw on the AD5X

On fbdev the main loop invalidates the whole screen every 10 s, to
paint over kernel console text that could show through. On the AD5X
nothing else draws on fb0: the 6.6 kernel's fbcon is held off by
KD_GRAPHICS, and the mainline 7.3 kernel has no VT or fbcon (printk
goes to the serial port only). The redraw only cost a full render and
copy into the uncached framebuffer every 10 s, during prints too.
---
diff --git a/src/application/application.cpp b/src/application/application.cpp
index 98ec3d8..1c2863d 100644
--- a/src/application/application.cpp
+++ b/src/application/application.cpp
@@ -2074,8 +2074,16 @@ int Application::main_loop() {
     // fbdev self-heal: periodic full-screen invalidation to overwrite any kernel
     // console text that bleeds through LVGL's partial render. KDSETMODE KD_GRAPHICS
     // is the primary defense; this is belt-and-suspenders for robustness.
+#if defined(HELIX_KILN_AD5X)
+    // Kiln OS (AD5X): nothing else draws on fb0. The 6.6 kernel's fbcon is
+    // held off by KD_GRAPHICS and the 7.3 kernel has no VT or fbcon at all
+    // (printk goes to the serial port only), so a full redraw every 10 s
+    // only costs CPU and memory bandwidth, also during prints.
+    bool needs_fb_self_heal = false;
+#else
     bool needs_fb_self_heal =
         m_display->backend() && m_display->backend()->type() == DisplayBackendType::FBDEV;
+#endif
     uint32_t last_fb_selfheal_tick = start_time;
     static constexpr uint32_t kFbSelfhealIntervalMs = 10000; // 10 seconds
 
